From 481487e36ba12f1d2065f6d262124bee4e55428b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:44:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Label the lazy ClearKey DRM service

The product installs the 1.4 lazy ClearKey service, while the default
file contexts only cover the legacy 1.0 DRM service names. The binary
therefore inherits vendor_file and init refuses to start it even in
permissive mode, leaving MediaDrm clients waiting for registration.

Assign the exact installed ClearKey path to the existing DRM HAL exec
type and reuse its domain transition without adding any allow rules.

Signed-off-by: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
---
 vendor/file_contexts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/vendor/file_contexts b/vendor/file_contexts
index 12e5d9f9798e1f7974e5948eea0898b0d20c99b2..653736fde6f84647197b2d19967d74796a4881ac 100644
--- a/vendor/file_contexts
+++ b/vendor/file_contexts
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.contexthub@1\.[0-9]+-service     u:object_r:hal_contexthub_default_exec:s0
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.drm@1\.0-service            u:object_r:hal_drm_default_exec:s0
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.drm@1\.0-service-lazy       u:object_r:hal_drm_default_exec:s0
+/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.drm@1\.4-service-lazy\.clearkey u:object_r:hal_drm_default_exec:s0
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.cas@1\.[0-2]-service            u:object_r:hal_cas_default_exec:s0
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.cas@1\.[0-2]-service-lazy       u:object_r:hal_cas_default_exec:s0
 /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.dumpstate@1\.[0-1]-service\.example      u:object_r:hal_dumpstate_default_exec:s0
